<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Unibanco 9-mo net 200.5 mln reais.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Unibanco 9-mo net 200.5 mln reais.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unibanco, Brazil's third-largest private bank, released the following consolidated earnings figures for the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>			Jan-Sept 1996	Jan-Sept 1995</p>
<p>    Net Profit	  200.5 million	   98 million</p>
<p>    Share Net	   2.11 reais	  N/A</p>
<p>    Net Fin Revs	1.6 bln	     N/A</p>
<p>    Net Worth	   2.1 bln	     1.2 bln</p>
<p>Note: All figures are in Brazilian reais. The figure for net profit is not adjusted for inflation.</p>
<p>Inflation-adjusted net for the firm reached 180.1 million reais in January-September 1996, a bank source said. No comparative figure for the same period last year was immediately available.</p>
<p>Unibanco has released the figures to Brazil's stock exchanges.</p>
<p>-- James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 248 5413</p>
